-- title:
--   Order bound for β(d)h^m on the α-fibre of an index place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$ and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$, together with $N\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $(N:K)\neq 0$, $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\neq p$. Write $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the subfield of $K((q))$ generated by `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`, and $R=$ `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ`, generated over $K$ by `jqModC K`, `jqNModC K N`, `jqNModC K ℓ` and `jqNModC K (N*ℓ)`; let $\alpha=$ `heckeAlphaC K N ℓ` (the inclusion $F\subseteq R$) and $\beta=$ `heckeBetaC K N ℓ` (the map induced by $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$), both assumed integral as ring homomorphisms. Let $m\ge 1$, let $h\in R$ and $d\in F$ be nonzero, and assume: at every place $z$ of $F$ over $K$ lying in `ssPlaces p N K` one has $\operatorname{ord}_z d\ge -(\,$`weightDivisor K N m`$\,)(z)$, the divisor whose value at each place is `weightFloor K N m`; and for every $z$ in `SSIndex p N K hp5 (2m)` — a supersingular place whose `placeWidth` divides $m$ — the value $z\bigl(\mathrm{unif}^{a(z)}d\bigr)$ vanishes, where $a(z)=$ `poleOrder p N K hp5 (2m) z` $=m\bigl(\,$`jWidth`$(z(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,K\,N))-1\bigr)/$`placeWidth`$(z)$. Fix such an index place $x$ and a finite set $S$ of places of $R$ characterised by $y\in S\iff y|_F=x$ along $\alpha$ (so $S$ is exactly the $\alpha$-fibre of $x$). Assume that for all $y\in S$: $\operatorname{ord}_y h=e_\beta(y)\,r(y|_F^{\beta})-e_\alpha(y)\,r(x)$ with $r=$ `placeRamificationJ N` and $e_\alpha,e_\beta$ the ramification indices along $\alpha,\beta$; $e_\alpha(y)\,u(y|_F^{\beta})=e_\beta(y)\,u(x)$ with $u=$ `placeWidth N`; and $y|_F^{\beta}$ lies in `ssPlaces p N K`. Then for every $y\in S$, $$\operatorname{ord}_y\bigl(\beta(d)\,h^{m}\bigr)\ \ge\ -e_\alpha(y)\,a(x)+1 .$$
--
--   This is the order estimate underlying the Hecke action on leading coefficients at supersingular places: it says that if a modular function $d$ satisfies the weight-$m$ floor conditions and has vanishing leads at all supersingular index places, then the correspondence transform $\beta(d)h^{m}$ has order strictly above the pole ceiling $-e_\alpha(y)a(x)$ at every place of the $\alpha$-fibre of a fixed index place $x$. It is used in the construction and the additivity and multiplicativity properties of the supersingular Hecke functional `ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.ssHeckeFun`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_neg_mul_poleOrder_add_one_le_ord_heckeBetaC_mul_pow.lean

